{"id":8182139,"docketId":65279759,"caseName":"Leman v. Eastman","caseNameFull":"Sheldon Dole Leman, Excutors, etc. v. Sidney C. Eastman, Trustee, etc.","slug":"leman-v-eastman","docketNumber":"No. 306","dateFiled":"1920-11-08","dateArgued":null,"dateCertGranted":null,"year":1920,"scdbId":"","direction":"","votesMajority":null,"votesMinority":null,"disposition":"","posture":"","syllabus":null,"summary":null,"headnotes":null,"proceduralHistory":null,"attorneys":null,"natureOfSuit":"","citationCount":0,"judges":"","jurisdictionType":"","opinions":[{"id":8144058,"type":"majority","typeCode":"020lead","perCuriam":false,"author":"","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":2370,"isHtml":true,"text":"<opinion type=\"majority\">\n<p id=\"Auc\">Error to the Supreme Court of the State of Illinois. Motions to dismiss submitted October 11, 1920. Decided November 8, 1920. <em>Per Curiam. </em>Dismissed for want of jurisdiction upon the authority of: (1) <em>Reetz </em>v. <em>Michigan, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"95797\"><a href=\"/opinion/95797/reetz-v-michigan/#508\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Reetz v. Michigan\">188 U. S. 505, 508</a></span>; <em>United States </em>v. <em>Heinze, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"97319\"><a href=\"/opinion/97319/united-states-v-heinze/#545\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: United States v. Heinze\">218 U. S. 532, 545-546</a></span>; <em>Lott </em>v. <em>Pittman, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"98925\"><a href=\"/opinion/98925/lott-v-pittman/#591\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Lott v. Pittman\">243 U. S. 588, 591</a></span>; <em>Ex parte Abdu, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"99166\"><a href=\"/opinion/99166/ex-parte-abdu/#30\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Ex Parte Abdu\">247 U. S. 27, 30</a></span>. (2) <em>Castillo </em>v. <em>McConnico, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"94793\"><a href=\"/opinion/94793/castillo-v-mcconnico/#683\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Castillo v. McConnico\">168 U. S. 674, 683</a></span>; <em>Standard Oil Co. </em>v. <em>Missouri, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"97608\"><a href=\"/opinion/97608/standard-oil-co-of-ind-v-missouri/#281\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Standard Oil Co. of Ind. v. Missouri\">224 U. S. 270, 281</a></span>; <em>McDonald </em>v. <em>Oregon Railroad &amp; Navigation Co., </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"98191\"><a href=\"/opinion/98191/mcdonald-v-oregon-railroad-navigation-co/#669\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: McDonald v. Oregon Railroad &amp; Navigation Co.\">233 U. S. 665, 669-670</a></span>; <em>Gasquet </em>v. <em>Lapeyre, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"98839\"><a href=\"/opinion/98839/gasquet-v-lapeyre/#369\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Gasquet v. Lapeyre\">242 U. S. 367, 369-370</a></span>. <em>Mr. Henry W. Leman </em>for plaintiffs in error., <em>Mr. Carl V. Wisner, </em>for Eastman, defendant in error. <em>Mr. Salmon O. Levinson, Mr. Benjamin V. Becker, Mr. Irwin T. Gilbruth </em>and <em>Mr. John P. Barnes, </em>for Northern Trust Company, defendant in error.</p>\n</opinion>"}],"citations":[]}